.TH SKYAPOD 1 "2026-10-01" "SkyAPO 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skyapod \- process a selected PipeWire capture stream with SkyAPO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skyapod
[\fB--config\fR \fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skyapod
is the per-user SkyAPO daemon. It connects to PipeWire, captures from the
selected source, runs the configured Equalizer APO-compatible DSP chain, and
publishes the processed stream as \fBSkyAPO Virtual Mic\fR.
.PP
The daemon can run directly in a terminal or through the installed systemd
user service. It does not require root. The realtime audio callback does not
parse configuration files or perform filesystem operations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Load \fIfile\fR instead of the per-user default configuration. If omitted,
the daemon uses \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skyapo/config.txt\fR, falling back to
\fB~/.config/skyapo/config.txt\fR when \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset.
.SH OPERATION
Select a PipeWire capture device with \fBskyapo device set\fR before starting
the daemon. The selected stable PipeWire node name is persisted in the
per-user configuration directory. Configuration changes are validated
outside the audio callback; a rejected reload keeps the last valid processing
chain active.
.PP
The daemon creates the virtual source \fBSkyAPO Virtual Mic\fR for normal
PipeWire clients. Status, control, and filter information are available from
the \fBskyapo\fR command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skyapo/skyapod.log
Log for a daemon started by \fBskyapo start\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/skyapo.sock
Mode-0600 per-user control socket.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/skyapod.service
Installed systemd user service (installation prefix may change this path).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Selects the per-user configuration root.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Selects the per-user runtime directory containing the control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skyapo (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wpctl (1)
